      "position": [
        2864,
        912
      ],
      "notes": "Same output shape as Do not proceed1 so the calling workflow needs no change."
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 0) Check the ticket is not already solved or closed\n\nRuns first, and on purpose does NOT post an internal note or reopen the ticket.\n\nWhy the guard: on 2026-07-23 Zendesk redelivered a `ticket created` webhook 8h37m late. The automation re-ran on the original first email, found the refundable charges already consumed, and emailed the customer a refund rejection after having already granted the refund.\n\nWhy no internal note here: the shared `Do not proceed` path sets the ticket back to `open`. On a solved ticket that would re-queue it for agents and could re-fire the 2nd-message trigger.\n\nWhy base `status` and not a `cs_project_config` id: the ticket API always returns `status` as a plain string, so no new column is needed and `closed` is covered for free.",
        "height": 340,
        "width": 460,
        "color": 3
      },
      "id": "39ad2cdd-25bf-4797-8963-3c9091c4e2a0",
      "name": "Sticky Status Guard",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        2464,
        1072
      ]
    }
  ],
